WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
<v Maya Chen>Quick check-in. Priya, you ran the load test on the queue?</v>

2
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:16.000
<v Priya Nair>Yes. It handled ten thousand events per minute with no backlog. Honestly, better than I expected.</v>

3
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.000
<v Daniel Brooks>Great news.</v>

4
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:33.000
<v Priya Nair>So I'll support the event-driven prototype going forward. Though if it gets messy in production, we should be able to switch back to batch quickly.</v>

5
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:39.000
<v Daniel Brooks>Sure, the batch fallback can stay in the codebase.</v>

6
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:45.000
<v Omar Haddad>CI is done. Every merge to main now deploys to staging.</v>

7
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:56.000
<v Maya Chen>Hosting: with MongoDB Atlas and the queue we're at three hundred and eighty dollars a month. That's close to the four hundred cap.</v>

8
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:02.000
<v Omar Haddad>If we need more, we'd have to ask the client.</v>

9
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:07.000
<v Maya Chen>Let's not touch it yet.</v>

10
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:15.000
<v Maya Chen>The runbook. Again, nobody owns it, and we go live in under two weeks.</v>

11
00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:20.000
<v Daniel Brooks>We really need it. I'm swamped though.</v>

12
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:25.000
<v Priya Nair>Same here.</v>

13
00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:30.000
<v Maya Chen>I'll raise it again on Friday.</v>

14
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:36.000
<v Daniel Brooks>Has anyone heard from Hussnain on the ingestion prototype?</v>

15
00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:42.000
<v Maya Chen>He's on billing, but the prototype is still his, due Friday.</v>

16
00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:47.000
<v Omar Haddad>I sent him the MongoDB credentials yesterday.</v>

17
00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:54.000
<v Maya Chen>Our data engineer contractor, Sam, starts Monday. Priya, can you onboard him?</v>

18
00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:59.000
<v Priya Nair>Yes, I'll onboard Sam.</v>

19
00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:08.000
<v Maya Chen>One more: the authentication provider. Do we use the client's existing single sign-on, or our own login?</v>

20
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:15.000
<v Daniel Brooks>Client single sign-on would be nicer, but we don't have their docs yet.</v>

21
00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:21.000
<v Maya Chen>Then that stays open until we get the docs.</v>

22
00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:26.000
<v Maya Chen>Thanks everyone.</v>
